# Status (2026-10-05): open. A splat cannot go to a user function's *rest parameter.
# Ruby: def diagonal(*vs); def scalar(n, v) = diagonal(*Array.new(n, v)) works (prints 3).
# Sake: "splat arguments go only to built-ins ...; hint: diagonal takes a fixed number of arguments",
# although it takes *vs (spec 5.8 still says user functions take a fixed number).
def diagonal(*vs) = Array.size(vs)
def scalar(n, v) = diagonal(*Array.new(n, v))
p(scalar(3, 7))
